 "fcrn_provenance_survey": {
  "_about": "Every human FcRn-containing entry returned by an RCSB text search for FcRn, plus the deposited unbound human Fc entries from the same experimental series. Each entry was screened for an IgG Fc chain and, where one is present, genotyped at the EU positions measured in contact with FcRn in 4N0U. Composition and title were confirmed against the RCSB entry and polymer-entity records.",
  "_finding": "Of the 9 FcRn-containing entries in this survey, 4 contain an IgG Fc chain (4N0U, 6WNA, 6WOL, 7Q15), and every one of those Fc chains is engineered at FcRn contact positions. None is wild type. The remaining FcRn entries are albumin or viral-capsid complexes with no Fc at all. Wild-type human IgG1 Fc has been solved unbound (4WI2, 6BZ4) but not, in this survey, bound to FcRn. Any statement about how wild-type IgG1 contacts FcRn is therefore inferred from engineered Fc, and the engineering sits inside the contact patch being measured.",
